  "body": "This is very useful from both functional and aesthetic standpoint for a lot of modern web apps which does authentication via a PIN sent to the user's phone number and/or email. It is also useful for inputs such as for credit card numbers.\r\n\r\nUsing `pattern=\"[0-9]+\"` helps at validation time which is good but the character is already present on the screen by then. `inputmode=\"numeric\"` only helps when virtual keyboards are present in phones and tablets and not when physical keyboards are being used. To get this functionality by hand at present seems to be extra work and one could inadvertently break keyboard accessibility as well.\r\n\r\nI know #1626 exists but I was hoping if we could look at this again since especially right now, PIN authentication is very popular in countries like India. This would also be helpful for building cleaved inputs and it would be nice to make these less error-prone and better visually.",
